|[[Evil Emperor Cat]]
|Judas
|scope="row" colspan="2"|Not only is he a traitor to the Cat Army, but [[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s Japanese name, Maō Hyōi (魔王憑依), translates to "Demon King Possession", and Judas is believed to have been possessed by Satan.
|-
|[[Possessed Empress]]
|Eve
|scope="row" colspan="2"|She appears in [[Aku's Melody (Merciless)|Temptation's Symphony]] and [[Temptation's Rhapsody]], is supported by [[Sinner Snache]] in [[Symphony of Bankruptcy (Merciless)|Symphony of Bankruptcy]], and her [[Empress' Research|pursuit of knowledge]] was what led to her to be possessed by an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]], similar to Eve being tempted by a serpent with the knowledge of good and evil.
|-
|[[Sathankhamun VIII]]
|Antichrist
|scope="row" colspan="2"|The Antichrist is sometimes interpreted as a human vessel in which Satan will [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|incarnate]]. In fact, the [[Media:Aku Reincarnation Event Poster JP.png|Japanese event poster]] for Rashomon contains the phrase ''Maō no Keshin'' (魔王の化身), meaning "Incarnation of the Demon King"". Moreover, one of the figures identified with the Antichrist is the eighth king in the Book of Revelation, explaining Sathankhamun VIII's name—it sounds similar to [[wikipedia:Tutankhamun|Tutankhamun]], a king, and contains the Roman numeral VIII (eight).
|-
|[[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]]
|Satan
|scope="row" colspan="2"|Design, stats and trait aside, the title he has instead of Infernal Tyrant in Japanese is ''Daimaō'' (大魔王), which translates to "Great Demon King"; Satan is an example of a ''[[wikipedia:ja:魔王|Maō]]'', which is occasionally even translated as "Satan" (e.g., [[Satan's Bedroom]]).
|-
|[[Xenobeast Bunaglios]]
|Lucifer and/or Abaddon
|scope="row" colspan="2"|Xenobeast Bunaglios was banished to a [[King of the Beasts: Final Bout (Brutal)|fiery pit in the wilderness]] where his tail appears to have grown long and heavy enough to take away his [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] trait, mirroring Lucifer's fall from Heaven. Lucifer's name means "light-bearer" or "light-bringer" and originally referred to the "morning star", the planet Venus as it appears at dawn, which may have inspired Bunaglios' glowing fists and horns and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] trait. His [[Explosion]] ability may be related to how Hell is associated with [[wikipedia:Sulfur|sulfur]], a component in gunpowder, which Lucifer creates in ''[[wikipedia:Paradise Lost|Paradise Lost]]''.<br>After his banishment, Bunaglios became feared as the king of all wild beasts, which could allude to Abaddon being the king of an army of locusts, and his destructive Explosions align with how Abaddon's name means "destruction". Sometimes Lucifer and Abaddon are identified with Satan, while other times they are regarded as their own beings.
|-
|[[Jumbo Jones]]
|Leviathan and/or the great fish
|scope="row" colspan="2"|Leviathan is a giant sea monster with various interpretations, such as Satan or one of the Princes of Hell, but also simply another of God's creations, which may be referenced by Jumbo Jones's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] trait. The [[Media:Bg016.png|ruined city background]] in [[Aqua Saint I (Deadly)|Aqua Saint I]] may imply that an apocalypse has occurred, which could be a reference to Leviathan being defeated at the end of time.<br>Jumbo Jones's Angel/[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] typing could also be inspired by the great fish sent by God to transport [[wikipedia:Jonah|Jonah]] by swallowing him.
|-
|[[Poultrio]]
|Asmodeus
|scope="row" colspan="2"|Poultrio is a three-headed devil, just like Asmodeus in the ''[[wikipedia:Dictionnaire Infernal|Dictionnaire Infernal]]''. In the same book, Asmodeus is portrayed with the leg of a rooster, which may be why Poultrio is named after poultry despite being an ostrich.
|}

