*Several of the Advent Bosses appear to be based on Japanese mythology:
**According to her Japanese description, the specific type of demon Hannya became is an ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'' (鬼). As such, she may have been inspired by the king of the ''oni'', [https://yokai.com/shutendouji/ Shuten dōji], who unwillingly became an ''oni'' after wearing a demonic mask to play pranks. It's said that Shuten dōji could survive even being reduced to a [https://data.ukiyo-e.org/harvard/images/HUAM-INV170251.jpg disembodied head], which is often depicted as red and massive like Hannya.
**Bakoo and Doremi are based on the ''[[wikipedia:Baku (mythology)|baku]]'', a dream-eating creature whose name can also refer to a [[wikipedia:Malayan tapir|Malayan tapir]].
**Kappy Jr. and [[Kappy Kawano]] are based on the ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'', an amphibious, reptilian, humanoid ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' with a penchant for cucumbers. Kappy Kawano may specifically represent [[wikipedia:Kuzenbo|Kuzenbo]], the king of the ''kappa''.
**Within the context of [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|Rashomon]], Sathankhamun VIII may represent [[wikipedia:Rashōmon no oni|Rashōmon no oni]], an ''oni'' said to have lived at the gate [[wikipedia:Rajōmon|Rashōmon]]. Sathankhamun VIII is a variant of Hannya, whose Japanese description refers to her as an ''oni''.
*Several of the Advent Bosses' genders are revealed outside of their English [[Enemy Guide]] entries:
**Cruel Angel Clionel is confirmed to be female by the [[Media:ClionelPoster.jpg|event poster]] for [[No Plan A (Deadly)|Clionel Ascendant]], which says, "Can you withstand her as she rains fire from long distance?!" Clionel is also called a mother (엄마 ''eomma'') in her Korean description.
**Hannya is confirmed to be female by an official [https://twitter.com/PONOS_EN/status/776236850591723520 Tweet] announcing [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|River Styx]], which reads: "Hannya has arrived in #BattleCats... dare you face her down in the new event stage River Styx? Log in on 9/15!"
**Daboo of the Dead is confirmed to be male by the [[Media:DeadonDebutPoster.jpg|event poster]] for [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Dead on Debut]], which says, "No seals, no curses, no spells can hold him back!"
**Masked Okame is confirmed to be female in her Korean description, which uses the feminine pronoun 그녀의 ''geunyeoui'' (her). In every version except [[BCEN]], Masked Okame is also stated to have a maiden's heart.
**Death Angel Z-Onel is confirmed to be female by the [[Media:Death Angel Z-Onel - Phantom Cat.png|event poster]] for [[Last of the Dead (Merciless)|Z-Onel Rises!]], which says, "Can you send this undying terror to her eternal rest?!"
**Doremi is confirmed to be female by her Korean name, Doremi Yang (도레미양), which can be taken as "Miss Doremi". When attached to a name, 양 ''yang'' is used for a girl or young woman, especially of lower age than the speaker; the masculine equivalent is 군 ''gun''.
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], the debut maps for Hannya and her other Advent Boss variants are all gates:
**Hannya: River Styx's Japanese name is Jigokumon (地獄門), meaning "Hell Gate".
**Masked Okame: Courts of Torment's Japanese name is Narakumon (奈落門), meaning "[[wikipedia:Naraka|Naraka]] Gate".
**Sathankhamun VIII: [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|Rashomon]] (羅生門) is another name of the fallen gate [[wikipedia:Rajōmon|Rajōmon]].
*Hannya is the first Advent Boss to appear in the main [[Legend Stages]] and the first to ever be fought above 100% strength magnification, both in [[Neutrino Snowlands]].
*Hannya, Kappy Jr. and Kappy Kawano are the only Advent Bosses to have neither Long Distance nor Omni Strike.
**While the Kappys both have powerful [[Surge Attack]]s, Hannya has no means of hitting units beyond her attack range.
*Kappy Jr. is the only Advent Boss to also appear in a different Advent Boss's main stage, spawning in both his own stage, [[Flow Like the Stream (Merciless)|Flow Like the Stream]], and in Kappy Kawano's [[Ghost King Finale (Brutal)|Ghost King Finale]].
*[[Evil Emperor Cat]] and [[Possessed Empress]] are the only Advent Bosses to be enemy versions of [[Cat Units]].
**In Evil Emperor Cat's case, this may be because he appears to have been designed as an [[Uncanny Legends]] enemy rather than an Advent Boss; see his article's trivia section for more information.
*In both [[The Battle Cats]] and [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Cruel Angel Clionel was the first ever Advent Boss.
*Daboo of the Dead being the fourth Advent Boss is likely a reference to how, in Japanese, one of the two pronunciations for the number 4 sounds exactly like the Japanese word for death. Moreover, he has four different immunities, his minimum money drop is 4,444, and his English name has four words while his Japanese name has four syllables (亡者デブウ, Mō-ja De-buu).
*The first four final bosses of the [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]] all have Advent Boss variants. [[The Face]] has Hannya, Masked Okame and Sathankhamun VIII; [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] has Evil Emperor Cat, Possessed Empress and Infernal Tyrant Nyandam; [[Teacher Bun Bun]] has Xenobeast Bunaglios; and [[Cli-One]] has Cruel Angel Clionel and Death Angel Z-Onel.
*[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]], [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] are tied for the most Advent Bosses of any enemy type, with four each.
*[[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] is the only standard enemy type to have no Advent Boss.

